[al:新概念英语第三册]
[ti:12. Life on a Desert Island]
[00:00.280] Passage 12 | 第12课
[00:01.455] Life on a Desert Island | 荒岛生活
[00:03.625] Most of us have formed an unrealistic picture of life on a desert island. | 我们大多数人对荒岛生活形成了一个不切实际的画面。
[00:08.850] We sometimes imagine a desert island to be a sort of paradise where the sun always shines. | 我们有时会把荒岛想象成一个阳光普照的乐园。
[00:15.015] Life there is simple and good. | 那里的生活简单而美好。
[00:17.475] Ripe fruit falls from the trees and you never have to work. | 成熟的水果从树上掉下来，你永远不必工作。
[00:22.030] The other side of the picture is quite the opposite. | 事情的另一面则恰恰相反。
[00:25.580] Life on a desert island is wretched. | 荒岛生活是悲惨的。
[00:28.150] You either starve to death, or live like Robinson Crusoe, waiting for a boat which never comes. | 你要么饿死，要么像鲁滨逊漂流记一样生活，等待一艘永远不会来的船。
[00:34.370] Perhaps there is an element of truth in both these pictures. | 也许这两种画面都有一定的真实性。
[00:38.200] But few of us have had the opportunity to find out. | 但我们中很少有人有机会去发现真相。
[00:41.475] Two men who recently spent five days on a coral island, wished they had stayed there longer. | 最近在珊瑚岛上度过了五天的两个人，希望他们能在那儿待更久。
[00:48.010] They were taking a badly damaged boat from the Virgin Islands to Miami to have it repaired. | 他们正把一艘严重受损的船从维尔京群岛开往迈阿密进行修理。
[00:54.730] During the journey, their boat began to sink. | 旅途中，他们的船开始下沉。
[00:58.100] They quickly loaded a small rubber dinghy with food, matches, and tins of beer, | 他们迅速将一艘小型橡皮艇装满食物、火柴和几罐啤酒，
[01:03.325] and rowed for a few miles across the Caribbean until they arrived at a tiny coral island. | 然后划了几英里穿过加勒比海，直到抵达一个微小的珊瑚岛。
[01:09.175] There were hardly any trees on the island, and there was no water, | 岛上几乎没有树，也没有水，
[01:13.500] but this did not prove to be a problem. | 但这并没有成为问题。
[01:16.235] The men collected rainwater in the rubber dinghy. | 男人们用橡皮艇收集雨水。
[01:19.970] As they had brought a spear gun with them, they had plenty to eat. | 因为他们随身带着一把鱼枪，所以他们有很多吃的。
[01:24.125] They caught lobster and fish every day, and as one of them put it, "ate like kings". | 他们每天都捕到龙虾和鱼，正如其中一人所说，“吃得像国王一样”。
[01:30.770] When a passing tanker rescued them five days later, | 五天后，当一艘路过的油轮救了他们时，
[01:34.375] both men were genuinely sorry that they had to leave. | 两人都真诚地感到遗憾，因为他们不得不离开。